.TH VIPER4LINUX-CTL 1 "November 2026" "ViPER for Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
viper4linux-ctl \- inspect and change live ViPER for Linux PipeWire processing controls
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B viper4linux-ctl
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B viper4linux-ctl --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Controls the currently running ViPER for Linux audio backend using its
shared-memory control channel. The backend must be running for commands other
than
.B --help
and
.BR -h .
Commands change the live processing controls. The GUI polls the shared
backend every 500 milliseconds and reflects CLI edits without restarting
audio. While the GUI is open, those edits are saved with its normal effect
settings. When the GUI is closed, CLI edits remain live in the backend, but
are not persisted until the GUI is reopened while that backend is still
running. A backend restart before then discards unsaved CLI changes. The CLI
does not manage named presets, IRS/VDC file selection, or window preferences. Exit status 0 indicates a successful command, 1 a missing backend, and
2 a usage or invalid-value error.
.PP
.B on
and
.B off
control the global ViPER processing bypass.
.B bass-on
and
.B bass-off
control only ViPER Bass. None of these commands starts or stops PipeWire.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Status and global processing
.TP
.B status
Print live control status, backend PID, sample rate, and audio block counter.
.TP
.BR on " | " off
Enable or bypass global effects. The native output limiter remains in the signal path.
.SS ViPER Bass and Bass Mono
.TP
.BR bass-on " | " bass-off " | " bass-toggle
Enable, disable, or toggle ViPER Bass (not the master bypass).
.TP
.BI "bass-mode " 0..2
0 Natural, 1 Pure Bass+, 2 Subwoofer.
.TP
.BI "gain " 0.5..10
Bass strength.
.TP
.BI "freq " 15..150
Bass frequency in Hz.
.TP
.BR mono-on " | " mono-off
Enable or disable Bass Mono.
.TP
.BI "mono-mode " 0..2
Bass Mono mode.
.TP
.BI "mono-strength " 0.5..10
Bass Mono strength.
.TP
.BI "mono-freq " 15..150
Bass Mono frequency in Hz.
.SS Psychoacoustic Bass and Dynamic System
.TP
.BR psycho-on " | " psycho-off
Enable or disable psychoacoustic bass.
.TP
.BI "psycho-cutoff " 60..150
Cutoff frequency, Hz.
.TP
.BI "psycho-intensity " 0..100
Effect intensity, percent.
.TP
.BI "psycho-order " 2..5
Harmonic order.
.TP
.BI "psycho-original " 0..100
Original-signal contribution, percent.
.TP
.BR dynamic-on " | " dynamic-off
Enable or disable Dynamic System.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-x-low " 0..2400
Low X crossover parameter.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-x-high " 0..12000
High X crossover parameter.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-y-low " 0..200
Low Y parameter.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-y-high " 0..300
High Y parameter.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-side-low " 0..100
Low-side gain, percent.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-side-high " 0..100
High-side gain, percent.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-strength " 0..100
Dynamic System strength, percent.
.SS Clarity and Spectrum Extension
.TP
.BR clarity-on " | " clarity-off
Enable or disable Clarity.
.TP
.BI "clarity-mode " 0..2
Native Clarity mode.
.TP
.BI "clarity-gain " 0..4.5
Clarity gain.
.TP
.BR spectrum-on " | " spectrum-off
Enable or disable Spectrum Extension.
.TP
.BI "spectrum-freq " 2200..8200
Spectrum reference frequency, Hz.
.TP
.BI "spectrum-exciter " 0..6
Exciter strength.
.SS Dynamic EQ, Tone, and device correction
.TP
.BR deq-on " | " deq-off
Enable or disable Dynamic EQ. Configure the individual frequency bands in the GUI.
.TP
.BR tube-on " | " tube-off
Enable or disable Tube Simulator.
.TP
.BI "tube-model " 0..2
Select the tube model (0 12AX7, 1 12AU7, 2 6N1P).
.TP
.BI "tube-drive " 0..100
Tube drive, percent (whole number).
.TP
.BI "tube-mix " 0..100
Tube mix, percent (whole number).
.TP
.BR analogx-on " | " analogx-off
Enable or disable AnalogX.
.TP
.BI "analogx-mode " 0..2
Mild, Medium, or Strong (whole-number index).
.TP
.BR ddc-on " | " ddc-off
Enable or disable ViPER-DDC. A compatible profile must already be selected
in the GUI; the command does not select an external .vdc file.
.TP
.BR speaker-on " | " speaker-off
Enable or disable Speaker Correction.
.SS Compressors and Stereo Imager
.TP
.BR fet-on " | " fet-off
Enable or disable the native FET compressor.
.TP
.BI "fet-threshold " -48..0
FET compressor threshold in dB (whole number).
.TP
.BI "fet-ratio " 1..10
FET compression ratio, in 0.1 increments.
.TP
.BR mb-on " | " mb-off
Enable or disable the native Multiband Compressor.
.TP
.BI "mb-bands " "3|5"
Choose three or five compressor bands. Configure individual band parameters
in the GUI.
.TP
.BR imager-on " | " imager-off
Enable or disable the three-band Stereo Imager.
.TP
.BI "imager-low " 0..200
Low-frequency stereo width, percent.
.TP
.BI "imager-mid " 0..200
Mid-frequency stereo width, percent.
.TP
.BI "imager-high " 0..200
High-frequency stereo width, percent.
.TP
.BI "imager-xover-low " 80..400
Low/mid crossover frequency in Hz.
.TP
.BI "imager-xover-high " 2000..8000
Mid/high crossover frequency in Hz.
.SS Cure Crossfeed
.TP
.BR crossfeed-on " | " crossfeed-off
Enable or disable ViPER Cure crossfeed.
.TP
.BI "crossfeed-mode " 0..2
Mild, Medium, or Strong crossfeed preset (whole-number index).
.SS Graphic equalizer and Convolver
.TP
.BR eq-on " | " eq-off
Enable or disable the native graphic EQ.
.TP
.BI "eq-bands " "10|15|25|31"
Select the active number of EQ bands. Unlike the GUI, the CLI does not maintain
separate saved EQ layouts per band count.
.TP
.BI "eq-level " "index dB"
Set a one-based band
.I index
(1 through the currently active band count) to a level from -12 to +12 dB.
.TP
.BR convolver-on " | " convolver-off
Enable or disable the Convolver; an actual impulse response must be loaded
through the GUI.
.TP
.BI "convolver-cross " 0..100
Cross-channel mix, percent.
.SS Spatial effects
.TP
.BR headphone-on " | " headphone-off
Enable or disable Headphone Surround+.
.TP
.BI "headphone-level " 1..5
Select Headphone Surround+ Level 1 through Level 5, matching the GUI exactly.
These are five distinct built-in surround filter profiles, not an objective
quality ranking. The backend stores levels as 0 through 4 internally, but
this internal numbering is not used for CLI arguments or status output.
For example,
.B viper4linux-ctl headphone-level 2
selects the GUI's Level 2. Only whole numbers 1 through 5 are accepted;
zero, fractions and out-of-range values return exit status 2 without changing
the setting.
.TP
.BI "headphone-quality " 1..5
Backward-compatible command-name alias for
.BR headphone-level .
The argument now follows the same 1 through 5 GUI numbering, not the old
0 through 4 scale. Scripts written for the previous CLI should increase the
argument by one when migrating.
.TP
.BR diff-on " | " diff-off
Enable or disable Differential Surround.
.TP
.BI "diff-delay " 1..20
Delay in milliseconds.
.TP
.BI "diff-reverse " 0|1
Reverse setting; integer 0 or 1.
.TP
.BI "diff-mix " 0..100
Wet mix, percent.
.TP
.BI "diff-lowpass " 0..20000
Low-pass cutoff in Hz.
.TP
.BR field-on " | " field-off
Enable or disable Field Surround.
.TP
.BI "field-widen " 0..8
Widening amount.
.TP
.BI "field-mid " 1..2
Mid image setting.
.TP
.BI "field-depth " "0|200..950"
Depth setting; 0 or 200 through 950.
.TP
.BR reverb-on " | " reverb-off
Enable or disable Reverberation.
.TP
.BI "reverb-room " 0..100
Room size, percent.
.TP
.BI "reverb-width " 0..100
Stereo width, percent.
.TP
.BI "reverb-damp " 0..100
Damping, percent.
.TP
.BI "reverb-wet " 0..100
Wet amount, percent.
.TP
.BI "reverb-dry " 0..100
Dry amount, percent.
.SS Output processing
.TP
.BI "limiter-threshold " 0.3..1
Native master limiter threshold, linear units.
.TP
.BI "limiter-gain " 0.01..2
Master output gain as a multiplier (1 = 100%).
.TP
.BI "limiter-pan " -1..1
Stereo balance; 0 centered.
.TP
.BR agc-on " | " agc-off
Enable or disable playback gain control (AGC).
.TP
.BI "agc-strength " 0.5..3
AGC strength.
.TP
.BI "agc-max " 1..10
Maximum AGC gain.
.TP
.BI "agc-threshold " 0.3..1
AGC output threshold.
.TP
.BR lufs-on " | " lufs-off
Enable or disable LUFS targeting.
.TP
.BI "lufs-target " -24..-8
Target loudness (LUFS).
.TP
.BI "lufs-max " 0..12
Maximum adjustment (dB).
.TP
.BI "lufs-speed " 0..2
LUFS response speed; integer 0, 1, or 2.
.SH COMPATIBILITY ALIASES
The older commands
.B all-on
and
.B all-off
remain accepted as aliases of the global
.B on
and
.BR off .
The older
.B toggle
command remains an alias of
.B bass-toggle
for compatibility with existing scripts.
.SH LIMITATIONS
The CLI does not currently provide controls for Stereo Imager, FET Compressor,
Multiband Compressor, Dynamic EQ, Tube Simulator, AnalogX, Cure/Crossfeed,
Speaker Correction, ViPER-DDC, IRS/VDC profile import and selection, named
presets, themes, or window/tray preferences. Some effects are controllable
through their live shared-memory interface but not through this CLI parser.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
viper4linux-ctl status
viper4linux-ctl off
viper4linux-ctl on
viper4linux-ctl bass-on
viper4linux-ctl bass-off
viper4linux-ctl gain 2
viper4linux-ctl eq-level 1 -2.5
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR viper4linux (1)
